@node OVERVIEW "Overview"
@{b}Overview@{ub}

Backup Vault is a job/Repository based backup utility, similar in
spirit to Veeam: you define a Repository (a destination) once, then one
or more Backup Jobs that write full, standalone archives (.bku) into
it. Separately, Sync Jobs keep two directories mirrored against each
other without going through the archive system at all.

The package is four programs sharing the same code and archive format:

  @{b}BackupVault@{ub}         - the MUI graphical front end (what this guide
                    mostly describes).
  @{b}Backup@{ub}              - a command-line tool for scripted use.
  @{b}BackupVaultDaemon@{ub}   - a headless scheduler, still in development.
  @{b}BackupVaultWebDaemon@{ub} - an experimental web browser/downloader for
                    Repository contents, still in development.

See @{" Programs in this package " LINK PROGRAMS} for all four, and
@{" Disclaimer " LINK DISCLAIMER} before relying on any of them for
anything you can't afford to lose.

Go back to the @{" main menu " LINK MAIN}.
@endnode


@node FEATURES "Features"
@{b}Features@{ub}

  - Job/Repository based backup - define a destination once, reuse it
    from any number of Backup Jobs.
  - Three Repository kinds: a plain local directory, an SMB (Windows/
    Samba) network share, or an SFTP (SSH) share - see
    @{" Repositories " LINK REPOSITORIES}.
  - A Credential Manager so an SMB/SFTP username and password only have
    to be typed in once and can be reused by any number of
    Repositories - see @{" Credentials " LINK CREDENTIALS}.
  - Full, standalone archives with three compression choices: none, a
    small built-in LZSS compressor, or real Deflate via the optional
    third-party z.library - see @{" Compression " LINK COMPRESSION}.
  - Optional per-job archive retention (keep only the last N archives,
    older ones deleted automatically after each successful run).
  - Optional per-job exclude patterns (semicolon-separated AmigaDOS
    wildcards) to skip matching files/folders anywhere in the source
    tree - see @{" Creating a Backup Job " LINK CREATEJOB}.
  - A free-space warning before a manually-started Backup Job, if the
    destination doesn't look big enough for the source - see
    @{" Creating a Backup Job " LINK CREATEJOB}.
  - Optional per-job virus scanning before backup, via the third-party
    xvs.library - see @{" Creating a Backup Job " LINK CREATEJOB}.
  - Optional per-job/per-Sync-Job scheduling - Daily, Weekly, Monthly,
    or a fixed interval - plus an optional WBStartup + iconified launch
    so scheduled jobs can run unattended - see
    @{" Scheduling " LINK SCHEDULING}.
  - Two-way and one-way Sync Jobs, independent of the Backup Job/
    archive system, with a Preview option to see exactly what a run
    would do without changing anything - see
    @{" Sync Jobs " LINK SYNCJOBS}.
  - Full Restore, selective Restore Files, Check (verify without
    restoring), and Import Backup - see @{" The Restore tab " LINK RESTORETAB}.
  - A History tab logging every backup/restore/sync/check/deletion,
    with search and per-run log viewing - see
    @{" The History tab " LINK HISTORYTAB}.
  - A command-line companion tool for scripted use - see
    @{" The command-line tool " LINK CLITOOL}.
  - Two headless companion tools still under active development - a
    scheduler daemon and an experimental web browser/downloader for
    Repository contents - see @{" Programs in this package " LINK PROGRAMS}.

Go back to the @{" main menu " LINK MAIN}.
@endnode


